# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# PRECEDENCE: an environment variable that is already set beats this file. .env is loaded
# with override=False, so a stale exported OPENAI_API_KEY silently wins and the value here
# is never read. A 401 with a known-good key in .env is almost always that. See README §2.
#
# LLM keys are OPTIONAL: the pipeline runs end-to-end with `python -m pipeline --no-llm`,
# which imports no LLM class at all and produces numerically identical artifacts (PRD §37).
# Keys are only needed for LLM mode, where the CrewAI crews write the narrative sections.
#
# The provider is chosen entirely by which key is set — no provider name is hard-coded in src/.
# The crews try OPENAI_API_KEY first, then ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. With neither set:
#   `python -m pipeline`            falls back to --no-llm, says so, and exits 0
#   `python -m pipeline --llm`      exits 2 without starting a run
#   `python -m crews.data_analyst`  exits 2 and points at --no-llm mode

OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# LiteLLM model id CrewAI should use, e.g. gpt-4o-mini or claude-sonnet-4-5.
# Unset means the default in src/crews/common.py.
# CREWAI_LLM_MODEL=
